B.Kj=new A.c9("Skat is played by three active players each hand (this app seats you against two computer opponents). The deck has 32 cards: \u2666 diamonds, \u2665 hearts, \u2660 spades and \u2663 clubs, each running Ace, 10, King, Queen, Jack, 9, 8, 7.",!1)
B.Kc=new A.fC("Card point values")
B.EL=s(["Card","Points"],t.s)
B.Gk=s(["Ace","11"],t.s)
B.EU=s(["10","10"],t.s)
B.Fz=s(["King","4"],t.s)
B.FY=s(["Queen","3"],t.s)
B.Gc=s(["Jack","2"],t.s)
B.EM=s(["9, 8, 7","0"],t.s)
B.Fo=s([B.Gk,B.EU,B.Fz,B.FY,B.Gc,B.EM],t.rj)
B.LV=new A.dw([1],t.Ih)
B.KJ=new A.l4(B.EL,B.Fo)
B.Ki=new A.c9("That totals 120 points across the deck. Winning a trick means collecting the card points in it \u2014 the goal is to end up controlling enough of those 120 points, not to win the most _tricks_.",!1)
B.Gf=s([B.Kj,B.Kc,B.KJ,B.Ki],t.d)
B.Lf=new A.fF("overview","Players & the deck",B.Gf)
B.Kq=new A.c9("Each of the three players gets ten cards; the remaining two cards form the **skat**, dealt face down to the table. Seats are named by their bidding order: **forehand** (leads the first trick if they become declarer), **middlehand** and **rearhand**.",!1)
B.Gn=s([B.Kq],t.d)
B.L7=new A.fF("dealing","Dealing",B.Gn)
B.Kk=new A.c9("Players bid for the right to become declarer, using a fixed ladder of numbers (18, 20, 22, 23, 24, 27, 30, 33, 35, 36, 40, 44, 45, 46, 48, 50, 54, 55, 59, 60\u2026). A bid states only a number \u2014 it does not commit to a particular game type yet, only that the bidder believes they can make a game worth at least that much (see [Scoring](#scoring) for how a game's value is worked out).",!1)
B.DQ=s(["**Middlehand calls first**, bidding a number to forehand, who either _holds_ (accepts, becomes the higher bidder for now) or _passes_.","Whoever survives that exchange then bids against **rearhand** the same way.","The bidding climbs the ladder one step at a time until two of the three players have passed.","The remaining player becomes **declarer**, playing alone against the other two.","If everyone passes without a single bid being held, the hand is a **pass-out** \u2014 no game is played and it is redealt."],t.s)
B.Ke=new A.qg(B.DQ)
B.Kf=new A.qh("The number reached in the auction is only a floor: the declarer must choose and announce a game whose calculated value is at least that high, or the bid is an [overbid](#overbid).")
B.G7=s([B.Kk,B.Ke,B.Kf],t.d)
B.Lc=new A.fF("bidding","The auction",B.G7)
B.KB=new A.c9("Once bidding ends, the declarer chooses one of two routes:",!1)
B.K9=new A.fC("Pick up and discard")
B.Kw=new A.c9("The declarer picks up the two skat cards, adding them to their hand (now 12 cards), then discards any two cards face down \u2014 these become the declarer's skat pile and count toward their score at the end of the hand, but are not played.",!1)
B.Ka=new A.fC("Hand game")
B.KE=new A.c9("The declarer instead leaves the skat untouched and plays with their original ten cards. This is riskier \u2014 the skat's two cards are unknown and count for the declarer either way \u2014 but it is required for certain announcements and raises the game's value (see below).",!1)
B.G3=s([B.KB,B.K9,B.Kw,B.Ka,B.KE],t.d)
B.L6=new A.fF("skat","Skat, hand games & discarding",B.G3)
B.Kn=new A.c9("After deciding on the skat, the declarer announces what they will play. Each game type has a **base value** used in scoring.",!1)
B.Kb=new A.fC("Suit games")
B.Ko=new A.c9("One suit is trumps. The four jacks are always the top trumps regardless of suit, ranking \u2663 > \u2660 > \u2665 > \u2666 among themselves; below them come the remaining cards of the trump suit in their usual order (A, 10, K, Q, 9, 8, 7). The other three suits play as plain side suits.",!1)
B.G5=s(["Trump suit","Base value"],t.s)
B.F0=s(["\u2666 Diamonds","9"],t.s)
B.Ff=s(["\u2665 Hearts","10"],t.s)
B.ER=s(["\u2660 Spades","11"],t.s)
B.FZ=s(["\u2663 Clubs","12"],t.s)
B.EK=s([B.F0,B.Ff,B.ER,B.FZ],t.rj)
B.KH=new A.l4(B.G5,B.EK)
B.K5=new A.fC("Grand")
B.Kx=new A.c9("Only the four jacks are trumps (in the same club\u2013spade\u2013heart\u2013diamond order); every other card plays in its own suit as a side suit. Base value **24**.",!1)
B.K7=new A.fC("Null")
B.Kt=new A.c9("The declarer contracts to lose _every_ trick. There are no trumps \u2014 all four suits rank Ace (high), 10, K, Q, J, 9, 8, 7 (low) \u2014 note the jack drops back into its own suit instead of being a trump. Null has a fixed value rather than a multiplier-based one, and comes in four forms:",!1)
B.EP=s(["Form","Value"],t.s)
B.FW=s(["Null (with discard)","23"],t.s)
B.EV=s(["Null hand","35"],t.s)
B.Ev=s(["Null ouvert (with discard)","46"],t.s)
B.Fr=s(["Null ouvert hand","59"],t.s)
B.Fv=s([B.FW,B.EV,B.Ev,B.Fr],t.rj)
B.KG=new A.l4(B.EP,B.Fv)
B.Ks=new A.c9("Null games are won or lost outright \u2014 there is no matador or level scoring.",!1)
B.EZ=s([B.Kn,B.Kb,B.Ko,B.KH,B.K5,B.Kx,B.K7,B.Kt,B.KG,B.Ks],t.d)
B.Ld=new A.fF("gametypes","Game types",B.EZ)
B.Ku=new A.c9("Forehand leads to the first trick. Players must follow the suit led if they can; if a trump is led, that means playing a trump (jacks count as the trump suit). A player with none of the suit led may play any card, including a trump, to try to win the trick. Highest trump wins the trick; if no trump was played, the highest card of the suit led wins. The winner of a trick leads the next one.",!1)
B.KA=new A.c9("After all ten tricks are played, each side counts the card points in the tricks it won. The declarer also adds the points in their skat pile (for a pick-up game) or the two skat cards, unseen, are simply added to the declarer's total (for a hand game).",!1)
B.DT=s([B.Ku,B.KA],t.d)
B.L8=new A.fF("play","Playing tricks",B.DT)
B.K4=new A.fC("Suit and grand games: making the game")
B.KD=new A.c9("To win a suit or grand game, the declarer needs **61 or more** of the 120 card points (the defenders win together if they hold the other 60+). The game's _value_ is then:",!1)
B.KF=new A.c9("`value = base value \xd7 multiplier`",!0)
B.K8=new A.fC("The multiplier")
B.Kl=new A.c9("The multiplier starts from the matador count and adds one for each of the following that applies:",!1)
B.FS=s(['**Matadors ("mit"/"ohne" N)** \u2014 the length of the unbroken run of top trumps the declarer holds or is missing, starting from the club jack. Holding the club jack counts _mit_ (with); missing it counts _ohne_ (without). This is always at least 1.',"**Game** \u2014 always counted (+1).","**Hand** \u2014 the declarer played without picking up the skat.","**Schneider** \u2014 one side held the other to 30 points or fewer.","**Schneider announced** \u2014 declarer called it in advance on a hand game.","**Schwarz** \u2014 one side won every trick.","**Schwarz announced** \u2014 declarer called it in advance on a hand game.","**Ouvert** \u2014 declarer's hand was played face up."],t.s)
B.Kd=new A.qg(B.FS)
B.Kr=new A.c9("The declarer must reach a game value at least as high as the number they won the auction with \u2014 see [Overbidding](#overbid).",!1)
B.K6=new A.fC("Null games")
B.Kh=new A.c9("No multiplier \u2014 the fixed value from the table above is scored directly. The declarer wins by losing every trick; taking even one trick loses the game.",!1)
B.G8=s([B.K4,B.KD,B.KF,B.K8,B.Kl,B.Kd,B.Kr,B.K6,B.Kh],t.d)
B.Lb=new A.fF("scoring","Scoring a game",B.G8)
B.Ky=new A.c9("**Schneider** means holding the opponent to 30 card points or fewer (equivalently, taking 90+ yourself). **Schwarz** means winning every one of the ten tricks. Both can happen naturally in any suit or grand game and add a step to the multiplier when they do.",!1)
B.Kv=new A.c9("On a **hand game**, the declarer may additionally _announce_ schneider, schwarz, or play **ouvert** (hand face up on the table for both defenders to see) before a card is played. An announcement raises the game's value further, but also raises the stakes: failing to deliver what was announced is scored as a loss.",!1)
B.Gp=s([B.Ky,B.Kv],t.d)
B.L9=new A.fF("announcements","Schneider, schwarz & ouvert",B.Gp)
B.Kp=new A.c9("Because the auction number is agreed before the game type is chosen, it's possible to win the bidding at a number your actual game can't reach \u2014 for example holding the bid to 30 but only being able to declare a game worth 27. This is an **overbid**. An overbid game is scored as a loss regardless of how the cards actually fell, and \u2014 like any lost game \u2014 is scored at the value of the (highest legal) game the declarer _announced_, doubled.",!1)
B.Kz=new A.c9("A lost game's penalty, in general, is:",!1)
B.Km=new A.c9("`penalty = \u22122 \xd7 game value`",!0)
B.KC=new A.c9("using whichever value is higher: the value the announced game would have scored if won, or the value needed to cover the bid.",!1)
B.EY=s([B.Kp,B.Kz,B.Km,B.KC],t.d)
B.Le=new A.fF("overbid","Overbidding",B.EY)
B.FR=s(["Game","Base","Trumps","Win condition"],t.s)
B.ES=s(["\u2666 Diamonds","9","Jacks + \u2666","61+ card points"],t.s)
B.DW=s(["\u2665 Hearts","10","Jacks + \u2665","61+ card points"],t.s)
B.Gl=s(["\u2660 Spades","11","Jacks + \u2660","61+ card points"],t.s)
B.EB=s(["\u2663 Clubs","12","Jacks + \u2663","61+ card points"],t.s)
B.Fc=s(["Grand","24","Jacks only","61+ card points"],t.s)
B.EG=s(["Null","23\u201359","none","lose every trick"],t.s)
B.FT=s([B.ES,B.DW,B.Gl,B.EB,B.Fc,B.EG],t.rj)
B.KI=new A.l4(B.FR,B.FT)
B.Kg=new A.qh("This app implements the full auction, hand games, pick-up-and-discard, all game types above, schneider/schwarz/ouvert announcements, matador and level scoring, overbid detection and the doubled loss. Variants such as Ramsch, Bock rounds, Kontra/Re, Revolution and Spitze are not included \u2014 see the project's `THIRD_PARTY.md` for details.")
